start:configfirewall_firewalld
description:configfirewall leaves firewalld running and enabled on the MN and on a CN, with the ports xCAT serves open on the provisioning NIC and on the public NIC of the MN. The case puts the firewall state of both nodes back at the end
label:firewall
os:rhels
cmd:/opt/xcat/share/xcat/tools/autotest/testcase/configfirewall/fw_check.sh save
check:rc==0
cmd:xdcp $$CN /opt/xcat/share/xcat/tools/autotest/testcase/configfirewall/fw_check.sh /tmp/fw_check.sh
check:rc==0
cmd:xdsh $$CN /tmp/fw_check.sh save
check:rc==0
cmd:sh -c 'T=/opt/xcat/share/xcat/tools/autotest/testcase/configfirewall; /install/postscripts/configfirewall --private "$($T/fw_check.sh nic-to __GETNODEATTR($$CN,ip)__)" --public "$($T/fw_check.sh nic-default)"'
check:rc==0
cmd:sh -c 'T=/opt/xcat/share/xcat/tools/autotest/testcase/configfirewall; $T/fw_check.sh check "$($T/fw_check.sh nic-to __GETNODEATTR($$CN,ip)__)" 22/tcp 3001/tcp 3002/tcp 69/udp 67/udp 80/tcp 443/tcp 2049/tcp 873/tcp'
check:rc==0
check:output=~FWCHECK-OK
check:output!~FWCHECK-BAD
cmd:sh -c 'T=/opt/xcat/share/xcat/tools/autotest/testcase/configfirewall; $T/fw_check.sh check "$($T/fw_check.sh nic-default)" 22/tcp 3001/tcp 3002/tcp 69/udp 80/tcp 443/tcp 873/tcp'
check:rc==0
check:output=~FWCHECK-OK
check:output!~FWCHECK-BAD
cmd:updatenode $$CN -P "configfirewall --auto"
check:rc==0
check:output=~configfirewall exited with code 0
cmd:xdsh $$CN "/tmp/fw_check.sh check \$(/tmp/fw_check.sh nic-default) 22/tcp 3001/tcp 3002/tcp 69/udp 67/udp 80/tcp 443/tcp 2049/tcp 873/tcp"
check:rc==0
check:output=~FWCHECK-OK
check:output!~FWCHECK-BAD
cmd:xdsh $$CN /tmp/fw_check.sh restore
check:rc==0
cmd:xdsh $$CN rm -f /tmp/fw_check.sh
cmd:/opt/xcat/share/xcat/tools/autotest/testcase/configfirewall/fw_check.sh restore
check:rc==0
end

start:configfirewall_nat
description:configfirewall --nat makes the MN masquerade out of its public NIC with firewalld running, and the CN then reaches the external network through the MN. The case first takes away any masquerade the MN had, and confirms the CN loses the external network, so the second reach can only come from configfirewall
label:firewall
os:rhels
cmd:/opt/xcat/share/xcat/tools/autotest/testcase/configfirewall/fw_check.sh save
check:rc==0
cmd:sh -c 'if systemctl is-active --quiet firewalld; then for z in $(firewall-cmd --get-zones); do firewall-cmd --zone=$z --query-masquerade >/dev/null && firewall-cmd --zone=$z --remove-masquerade >/dev/null; firewall-cmd --permanent --zone=$z --query-masquerade >/dev/null && firewall-cmd --permanent --zone=$z --remove-masquerade >/dev/null; done; fi; true'
check:rc==0
cmd:xdsh $$CN "curl -sS -m 30 -o /dev/null -w CNEXT=%{http_code} http://1.1.1.1/"
check:output!~CNEXT=[1-5][0-9][0-9]
cmd:sh -c 'T=/opt/xcat/share/xcat/tools/autotest/testcase/configfirewall; /install/postscripts/configfirewall --private "$($T/fw_check.sh nic-to __GETNODEATTR($$CN,ip)__)" --public "$($T/fw_check.sh nic-default)" --nat'
check:rc==0
cmd:sh -c 'T=/opt/xcat/share/xcat/tools/autotest/testcase/configfirewall; $T/fw_check.sh masquerade "$($T/fw_check.sh nic-default)"'
check:rc==0
check:output=~FWCHECK-OK
check:output!~FWCHECK-BAD
cmd:xdsh $$CN "curl -sS -m 30 -o /dev/null -w CNEXT=%{http_code} http://1.1.1.1/"
check:rc==0
check:output=~CNEXT=[23][0-9][0-9]
cmd:/opt/xcat/share/xcat/tools/autotest/testcase/configfirewall/fw_check.sh restore
check:rc==0
end
